	(text "MCU: ESP32-C3 Rust board A1 (DevKit-RUST-1 Rev 1.2a fitted, RUST-2 fits) in gold socket headers (D-93 to D-95). Net labels at the DevKit pins.\n3V3 pin from U11 (LDO); EN low keeps the board buck off;\n5V/VBUS not connected, so the PC can stay on USB (board diode D6). Wi-Fi and BLE off in firmware.\nI2C: board bus SDA GPIO10 (RUST-1) or GPIO7 (RUST-2), set by JP11 (2-3 or 2-1, D-94); SCL GPIO8. 10k on the board; 2.2k on the RF board.\nGPIO0 EXP_INT, GPIO1 WDI (kick at least every 0.9 s), GPIO3 LATCH_CLR (rising edge), GPIO4 MCU_EN_N (low = relays allowed),\nGPIO5 KILL (read), GPIO6 FAULT (read, 1k R66, D-191), GPIO20/21 UART 9600 baud. GPIO2, 8, 9 are strapping pins: GPIO2 and GPIO9 not used; GPIO8 is SCL.\nBoard LED on GPIO7 (RUST-1) or GPIO10 (RUST-2): the SDA pin of the other board.\nSafety gate (D-59): RLY_EN = NOR(KILL, MCU_EN_N, FAULT). FAULT is set by RESET_N: power-up, 3V3 below 2.83 to 3.00 V, or no WDI edge for 0.9 to 2.5 s.\nAfter a reset the relays stay off until the MCU gives a LATCH_CLR edge. KILL is not latched. RLY_EN has a 100k pull-down on the RF board.\nREADY_ON = NOR(MCU_EN_N, FAULT) (U15, D-62): closes the READY switch in the SAFE loop. Start-up: LATCH_CLR, MCU_EN_N low, then KILL reads 0 (F11).\nU12 RESET_N does not reset the MCU (DevKit pin 1 RST open); the ESP32-C3 has its own watchdogs. MR open: internal 90k pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
